=== SURVEY (web source read end-to-end) ===
FreshnessIndicator.tsx renders the age of a SPECIFIC datum: a small coloured dot + an optional
relative-time label, sized off a `timestamp` prop and a 10s re-render `setInterval`.
  • FreshnessStatus union: fresh | stale | offline | unknown.
  • computeAge(ts): null when !ts; else max(0, floor((now - ts_ms)/1000)).
  • getStatus(age, stale=120, offline=600): null→unknown; <stale→fresh; <offline→stale; else→offline.
  • formatAge(age): null→"—"; <10→"just now"; <60→"{n}s ago"; <3600→"{n}m ago"; else "{n}h ago".
  • DOT_COLOR: fresh=neon-green, stale=neon-amber, offline=neon-red, unknown=var(--surface-2).
  • DOT_SIZE: sm=6px, md=8px.  LABEL_SIZE: sm=10px, md=12px.  fresh → animate-pulse.
  • Render: span(inline-flex gap-1, title=timestamp){ dot; showLabel && muted label }.
  • Exported hook useIsStale(ts, stale=120) → { isStale: age>=stale, isOffline: age>=600, ageLabel }.
The component is anonymous — it has NO t() calls (hardcoded English literals). Per the prompt, every
literal is lifted into the P1/S10 facade with the verbatim web text as the fallback value.
Data sources (P1/S8): useIsStale. Shared components: none. Charts/maps: none.
Existing native: the ATOMIC primitive `TSFreshnessIndicator` (Sources/Components/DataDisplay/
StatusIndicators.swift) is the component-library peer and is OUT OF SCOPE here; this surface is the
distinct shared-surface `FreshnessIndicator` (no symbol collision — verified). Canonical surface
pattern studied: shared-surfaces/AIChatbotIndicator (Adapter/Projection/Model/Views/swift/Previews/
strings/Tests).

=== REASONING / IMPLEMENTATION ===
Mirrors the AIChatbotIndicator leaf architecture, adapted to the freshness data + 10s tick:
  • Adapter.swift  (pure, Foundation): FreshnessResolve i18n seam; FreshnessStatus; FreshnessSize
    (dotDiameterPoints 6/8 = web DOT_SIZE); FreshnessThresholds (120/600 web defaults); FreshnessAge
    (verbatim computeAge: nil/empty/malformed→nil, future→0 clamp, ISO-8601 w/ + w/o fractional
    seconds, whole-second floor); FreshnessStatusResolver (verbatim getStatus); FreshnessAgeFormatter
    (verbatim formatAge, i18n-routed, %@-token number insertion); FreshnessStaleEvaluator (verbatim
    useIsStale); FreshnessIndicatorMeta (slug + 10s tick cadence); FreshnessAccessibility.
  • Projection.swift: FreshnessFetchStatus (loading/resolved/failed) + FreshnessInput (timestamp feed);
    FreshnessConfig (web non-data props: thresholds/showLabel/size); FreshnessReadout; FreshnessResolved
    {phase: loading|unavailable|ready(readout), stale: useIsStale verdict}; pure FreshnessProjection.
  • Model.swift (P1/S8 + S10 + S11): FreshnessTelemetry seam + OSLog default; FreshnessIndicatorSource
    seam + Live/InMemory sources; injected FreshnessClock (deterministic tests); FreshnessStrings i18n
    facade; @MainActor @Observable FreshnessIndicatorModel — start/stop/refresh/tick, lazy once-only
    view.opened on first .ready, one-shot auto-refresh on the fresh→stale transition (re-armed after
    leaving stale; an offline jump never arms it).
  • Views.swift: FreshnessDot (web DOT_COLOR tones via Color.TS.status*, fresh animate-pulse honouring
    Reduce Motion), FreshnessLabel, FreshnessReadyView (dot + optional label + web `title` tooltip +
    combined VoiceOver label), FreshnessLoadingChip (TSSkeleton), FreshnessUnavailableChip (TSButton
    retry — QueryError peer).
  • FreshnessIndicator.swift: phase switch; onAppear/onDisappear start/stop; 10s tick via a
    main-run-loop Timer publisher + .onReceive (Swift-6-safe: .onReceive's action is a main-actor,
    non-@Sendable closure, so it calls the @MainActor model directly; a .task @Sendable loop cannot
    cross into the actor under -strict-concurrency=complete).
  • Previews.swift (DEBUG): loading / unavailable / fresh / stale / offline / empty / md+label-hidden.
  • strings: table "FreshnessIndicator" — every web literal as the fallback value (no English in code).
  • AdapterTests.swift + Tests.swift: adapter unit tests; projection per-phase; model behaviour
    (telemetry-once, stale auto-refresh + re-arm, offline-no-refresh, clock-driven tick transition,
    start/stop/refresh); Live source; view composition per state; accessibility labels.
States rendered (every one — no hidden surface): loading (skeleton chrome), error/unavailable (retry
chip = QueryError peer), empty (resolved + nil timestamp → unknown status: neutral dot + "—",
VoiceOver "No data" — never a blank box), stale (amber dot + "{n}m ago" + one-shot auto-refresh),
offline (red dot, last-known "{n}h ago"), fresh (pulsing green dot + label).

